      "press_kit_debunking": "Boston models (especially Colleagues 1, 10, 11, 16, 17) directly countered the press kit/Variety argument by pointing out that David Rooney's September 1997 Variety review and Venice dossiers do not mention NYC, and that trivia evaluates canonical narrative text rather than imaginary English misprints."
    },
    "nyc_camp_performance": {
      "strengths": "Colleagues 5, 9, 13, and 14 executed a near-flawless tactical pivot: fully conceding the spoken Italian script ('lo mando a studiare a Boston') to disarm textual attacks, and focusing entirely on the meta-epistemic argument of trivia test construction, the 15–3 Round 0 distribution, and the specific phrasing 'moves to' vs. 'father decrees'.",
      "weaknesses": "Colleague 8 unfortunately repeated the specific claim that Tommaso 'explains when he returns to Livorno... he relocated to New York City', which Boston defenders continue to hammer as a factual lie."
    }
